# =============================================================================
# KrishiMitra frontend (Next.js) environment
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. In production these are set in
# the Vercel dashboard (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables).
#
# This file covers the FRONTEND only. The FastAPI service has its own variable
# surface (AGROTECH_*) documented in ml-service/.env.example — those belong on
# the Hugging Face Space, not on Vercel.
#
# Deployment topology:
#   Frontend  -> Vercel               (this app)
#   API       -> Hugging Face Spaces  (Docker SDK, listens on $PORT=7860)
#   Database  -> Neon                 (serverless Postgres, API side only)
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODE A (recommended, and the default) — same-origin proxy, no rebuild needed
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave NEXT_PUBLIC_ML_API_URL UNSET. The browser then calls the relative path
# /api/ml/*, which is served by app/api/ml/[...path]/route.ts and forwarded
# server-side to ML_API_URL.
#
# ML_API_URL is a plain (non-public) RUNTIME variable: it is read on every
# request, so the deployment can be repointed at a different backend by editing
# it in the Vercel dashboard and redeploying — no source change, no rebuild of
# the client bundle.
#
# Because the browser only ever sees a relative path, this mode also means:
#   * no CORS preflight between the two hosts, and
#   * the API hostname never appears in the shipped JavaScript.

# Local development. This is also the built-in default when unset, so a fresh
# clone runs with zero configuration: `npm run dev` + `npm run dev:ml`.
ML_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Hugging Face Space (production). The URL is derived from the Space owner and
# name — no trailing slash, no /api suffix:
# ML_API_URL=https://<hf-username>-<space-name>.hf.space
#
# Local docker compose uses the service name on the compose network:
# ML_API_URL=http://api:8080

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODE B — direct browser -> API calls. Leave this UNSET.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are INLINED INTO THE CLIENT BUNDLE at build time. Setting
# this bakes the API origin into the JavaScript that every visitor downloads,
# which means:
#   * changing the backend URL requires a full rebuild + redeploy, not just an
#     env-var edit — the whole reason the proxy in Mode A exists;
#   * the Space must allow the frontend origin in AGROTECH_CORS_ORIGINS, and
#     every request pays a CORS preflight;
#   * a localhost value would be catastrophic — every visitor's browser would
#     call their OWN machine.
#
# The one thing it buys is skipping the proxy hop, which sidesteps Vercel's
# 4.5 MB request-body limit on file uploads (see below). Only worth it if large
# uploads become a real problem.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ML_API_URL=https://<hf-username>-<space-name>.hf.space

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Port the Next.js server binds to.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Injected by the host. Not used on Vercel (it runs the app as functions, not as
# a long-lived server); relevant for `next start`, docker compose, and any other
# self-hosted run.
# PORT=3000

# =============================================================================
# Operational notes for the Vercel deployment
# =============================================================================
# Region (vercel.json -> "regions"): bom1 (Mumbai) keeps the server hop close to
# Indian users. If the Hugging Face Space turns out to be slow from bom1 — HF
# runs in AWS us-east-1 — iad1 puts the proxy next to the Space instead and may
# be faster end to end, since static assets are served from Vercel's CDN
# regardless of function region. Measure before changing it.
#
# Cold starts: a free Hugging Face Space scales to zero after ~48h idle and can
# take 30+ seconds to wake. The proxy waits up to 50s for response headers
# (maxDuration 60s) and then returns 504 with a "still waking up, retry"
# message rather than hanging or dying with an opaque platform error.
#
# Upload size: requests through the proxy pass through a Vercel Function, which
# caps the REQUEST BODY at 4.5 MB. The pest-detection page accepts
# `image/*,.pdf`, and an unresized phone photo routinely exceeds that — such a
# request is rejected by the platform before this app's code runs. Options:
# resize client-side before upload, or switch that one call to Mode B.
